WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.200
An architect's dream 
is firstly

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.120
to be identified by
developers with major projects

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.720
- that is
what all of us want -

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:56.160
and then there's the exploratory,
detective work

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.240
which aims to capture the essence of the location:

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:05.120
What the site 
chosen by the main developer

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.360
can,
or cannot offer.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.560
Well, there is something curious about this site, 
by the rue de la Loi,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.160
which is - let's face it -
a car-filled sewer...

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.240
Look at where similar buildings are found
around the world...

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.240
usually at the end
of a lengthy vista,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.560
flanked by umpteen rows of trees,
and facing due south,

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:30.400
carefully designed
to catch the eye.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:38.440
But the Council is staying put,
at the heart of this area.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.200
Alongside a road
with little architectural merit.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.960
Surrounded by functional buildings.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.440
It's moving... in its modest way.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.120
It certainly moved me;
I found it astonishing,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.960
to put such an important building
in such an incongruous place....

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.600
so that was my starting-point.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.400
The site is occupied by a building

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:13.040
that is one of Brussels' cultural landmarks:
the Résidence Palace.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:19.880
From the start I was determined
to try to save

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.080
most of the features 
of the historical part of the building.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.200
We looked,
in some detail,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.320
at what this old carcass
could still offer.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.600
It was immediately clear
that what was needed was a cube.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:42.240
There could be no half measures
or concessions on the shape,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.720
no frills and spills.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:49.920
Because all that would have spoilt
the symbolic aspect of this cube.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.720
It's a box, and a box is,
by definition, something that you open,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:55.920
otherwise it's a block.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:00.920
We had to make these façades "breathe".
And that was when it came to me...

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.240
We will make one façade
from old, recycled oak frames,

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.320
the sort you can find these days
in containers

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.880
in streets all over Europe.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.360
That allows us to send
a number of messages at once:

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:21.440
diversity - patchwork - unity,

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.160
after all, they are all frames
and they all have the same function,

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.640
all made of the same material - oak -
which you can find anywhere in Europe.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:34.360
and, what's more, there's the need to recycle.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.560
What's going to be the main concern
for our children and grandchildren?

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.520
It's clearly those questions - environmental questions - 
that will come first.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:48.760
And they'll be tackled in a much more generous,
inspiring, spontaneous way...

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:54.120
than our current,
remarkably timid approach.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.720
When we needed to get down
to the final preparations,

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:02.400
the first idea I had was
to make an open vase,

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.520
like a corolla of flowers.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.360
That was the first sketch.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.840
And then we started
looking at the surface,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.920
which led, bit by bit,
to its becoming what was called,

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.120
firstly, a callipygian goddess,
until it assumed its current form

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.600
which is being described as a "heart".

